# Non-source artifacts.
_book/
_bookdown_files/

# Left by `purl()`/`source()` runs from a directory-wide test, and by knitr's
# default graphics device when a chunk has no `dev` set. Neither is a source
# file; both appear the moment someone executes a chapter outside `render_book()`.
Rplots.pdf
figure/
knitrdir/

# Knitr cache / figure side directories produced by local renders.
# `docs/sclet_cache` is the redirect target of `cache.path` set in `.Rprofile`
# (enabled by `R_BOOKDOWN_RENDER=1`, which `make gitbook` exports).
sclet_cache
sclet_files

# `docs/` is a separate gh-pages checkout: its own git repository holding 22 MB
# of built HTML, with `.git/HEAD -> refs/heads/gh-pages`. It stays listed here
# so that rendering artefacts that land inside it stay invisible to git rather
# than showing up as untracked files in the published-site checkout.
#
# Building into it is still wrong: local renders go to `_book/` (see
# `output_dir` in `_bookdown.yml`), and CI renders into `../site` and pushes
# from there. `.Rprofile` writes only to the ignored `docs/sclet_cache/`.
# Never `git rm` this directory.
docs

# `gh-pages` and `sclet.Rmd` were historical leftovers with no corresponding
# file; they are gone.

# A full local render (render_book with an explicit output_dir), kept out of
# git the same way `_book/` is.
_book_full/
